  "query_preview": "..Much drier air begins to filter into the region \ntoday as low pressure drifts through the northern Great Basin \nheading into the weekend. Some remnant moisture over the eastern \nzones may lead to scattered showers and thunderstorms for one more \nday, but that is about it.\n\nThese remnant chances are gone over the weekend as dew points drop \ninto the lower 20s. Expect crisp and cool weather, due to overnight \nlows falling into the 30s. Daytime highs will remain at or just \nabove normal.\n\nBy early next week, another low  drifts over the area. This low may \ntake a southerly track, which may pick some of the Monsoon moisture \npool back up. We have added some low PoPs next week as this low \narrives, possibly even lasting through the rest of next week, as \nsoutherly flow returns. Confidence is marginal on this scenario, we \nwill wait and see.",
